{
  "baseline": "6136f1aa has the same JoySheet sources as 577d86b5. The retained baseline CLI originates from this unchanged Sheet source. The release microbenchmark uses 577d86b5 with the same driver for both versions.",
  "reference": "Microsoft Excel for Mac 16.115 fully recalculated and separately saved the two constructed reference workbooks. A1 changes from 7 to 12. Worksheet XML and cached numeric, text and error values were retained; author and local workbook-path properties were removed. Numeric comparisons have zero tolerance. Empty strings, padding, exact error types and formulas are checked separately.",
  "implementation": "Twelve signed binary, decimal, octal and hexadecimal conversions, five 48-bit operators and two variable-radix conversions share one first-party implementation. The 77 Unicode decimal-digit blocks in the probe include the ASCII and 18 other scripts recognized for numeric arguments by this Excel build. Encoded digits are ASCII. The reference covers signed ten-digit inputs, omitted and explicit width, 48-bit bounds, argument-error order, long UTF-16 strings and rounding above 2^53.",
  "timing": "Six public worksheet results are asserted before timing. Both optimized programs dispatch via the normal registry. Each series contains 11 interleaved runs of 100,000 calls. Units are nanoseconds per call. These timings measure the function kernel.",
  "rollback": "Rebuild 6136f1aa or restore the affected registrations and implementations from it. Both readers recalculate either writer’s workbook. The earlier reader reproduces the recorded numeric, text and error differences. Raw user workbooks have no formulas and are independently retained.",
